(1) run download.sh
(2) run filter_replays.py
(3) in parent, run replay_headless.py to regenerate tick logs (no browser, parallel)
(4) run create_bundles.py
(5) run create_item_touches.py
(6) run bundle.py

From the repo root, `bash run_analysis.sh` runs the full pipeline and writes `analysis/score_distributions.png`.

Use `SKIP_DOWNLOAD=1 ./run_analysis.sh` to reuse existing `replays_raw` files and start at filtering.

`download.sh` disables gsutil multiprocessing on macOS to avoid Python fork crashes.

Tick logs are generated by `replay_headless.py` (repo root), which drives the same
engine/game/replay path as the old server+browser flow (`main_replay.py` /
`auto_replay_loop.py`) but with no Flask/SocketIO server, no browser, and no per-tick
state emit. It is much faster and processes replays in parallel. Tick-log output is
byte-identical to the old flow except for a pre-existing quirk: the 3 team-`Score`
columns and the 1 `message` column carry a random object id in their *name* (their
values are identical) — the browser flow produced the same random-id columns.
The engine advances with a fixed `dt = 1/tick_rate`, so wall-clock speed never affects
the data; `tick_rate` stays pinned at the recorded 24 Hz (changing it would re-time
every step). `run_analysis.sh` skips replays that already have a CSV.

  - `REPLAY_JOBS` (default: CPU cores - 1, capped at 8) parallel worker processes.

Standalone use: `python replay_headless.py --jobs 8` (all pending), `--force`
(regenerate existing), `--only <file>` and `--out-dir <dir>` (single replay to a
scratch dir, useful for verification). The old `auto_replay_loop.py` is kept for
watching a replay render live in a browser.

`filter_replays.py` rebuilds `analysis/replays` from `replays_raw` each run (it clears the folder first). Inclusion is gated by these env vars, all optional:

  - `MAP_PREFIX`         (default empty = all maps) keep only maps whose `map_nr` starts with this prefix.
  - `INCLUDE_ENCOURAGED` (default 1) set 0 to drop `encouraged_*` maps.
  - `COLLISION_ONLY`     (default 1) keep only runs whose `additional_condition_info` contains "collision"; set 0 to include non-collision runs.
  - `ALLOWED_CONDITIONS` (default `mixed,optimal,superstar,asymetric_slow_walker,mixed_extreme`) comma-separated condition names to keep; set empty to allow all (including unrecognized combos labeled "other").

Condition names are assigned by `_condition_name()` from the per-player cutting/walking speeds. Files that are dropped, and why, are logged to `analysis/filter_report.json` (`excluded_condition` is the condition gate above).

Example — include everything regardless of map/collision/condition:

    MAP_PREFIX= COLLISION_ONLY=0 ALLOWED_CONDITIONS= ./run_analysis.sh